    {
      "id": "oHT7Wyg_YooUNGR-KP-Fj",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 953,
      "y": 146,
      "width": 692.9990844726562,
      "height": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 2,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2F",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 263684428,
      "version": 36,
      "versionNonce": 1034652148,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1757915244512,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "* Explain the memory layout differences between arrays and \nlinked lists. How does this impact cache performance, and when \nwould you choose one over the other in a high-performance \nsystem?\"",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "* Explain the memory layout differences between arrays and \nlinked lists. How does this impact cache performance, and when \nwould you choose one over the other in a high-performance \nsystem?\"",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "5NO0AQvgvHrHzjpaX1lDk",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 955,
      "y": 255,
      "width": 780.9991455078125,
      "height": 750,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 2,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2G",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1810423412,
      "version": 569,
      "versionNonce": 7633996,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1757915938589,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- Memory layout analysis:\n    - arrays: contiguous memory allocation with predctable addr.\n    - linked list: scattered memory allocation with pointer \n    navigation\n\n- Array memory layout:\n    - [data1, data2, data3, data4] ---- contiguous blocks\n      0X100   0X104  0X108  0X10C\n\n- Linked list memory layout:\n    - [data1|ptr] -> [data3|ptr] -> [data2|ptr] -> [data4|null]\n      0x200          0x350           0x180           0x420\n\n-Cache Line Impact:\n    - Array: Loading one element brings neighbors into cache \n    (spatial locality)\n    - Linked List: Each access may cause cache miss \n    (poor spatial locality)\n\n- Time/Space Complexity Analysis:\n    - Array Access: O(1) with high cache hit probability\n    - Linked List Access: O(n) with potential cache misses at each step\n    - Memory Overhead: Array = 0%, Linked List = 50-100% \n    (pointer overhead)\n\n- Pattern Recognition:\n    - Use arrays when: Sequential access, cache performance \n    critical, memory constrained\n    - Use linked lists when: Frequent insertions/deletions, \n    unknown size, non-sequential access",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- Memory layout analysis:\n    - arrays: contiguous memory allocation with predctable addr.\n    - linked list: scattered memory allocation with pointer \n    navigation\n\n- Array memory layout:\n    - [data1, data2, data3, data4] ---- contiguous blocks\n      0X100   0X104  0X108  0X10C\n\n- Linked list memory layout:\n    - [data1|ptr] -> [data3|ptr] -> [data2|ptr] -> [data4|null]\n      0x200          0x350           0x180           0x420\n\n-Cache Line Impact:\n    - Array: Loading one element brings neighbors into cache \n    (spatial locality)\n    - Linked List: Each access may cause cache miss \n    (poor spatial locality)\n\n- Time/Space Complexity Analysis:\n    - Array Access: O(1) with high cache hit probability\n    - Linked List Access: O(n) with potential cache misses at each step\n    - Memory Overhead: Array = 0%, Linked List = 50-100% \n    (pointer overhead)\n\n- Pattern Recognition:\n    - Use arrays when: Sequential access, cache performance \n    critical, memory constrained\n    - Use linked lists when: Frequent insertions/deletions, \n    unknown size, non-sequential access",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
