      "text": "* Explain XOR linked lists. Derive the mathematical foundation \nand discuss when this optimization is worthwhile despite \nincreased complexity.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "* Explain XOR linked lists. Derive the mathematical foundation \nand discuss when this optimization is worthwhile despite \nincreased complexity.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "yp_k_fjVLwEC01QY4iKqs",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1750.5004272460938,
      "y": 224,
      "width": 941.2452392578125,
      "height": 1175,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 2,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2L",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1778380492,
      "version": 727,
      "versionNonce": 1297600588,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1758089052802,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- Methematical Foundation:\n    - xor property: a ⊕ a = 0 and a ⊕ 0 = a\n\n- XOR Linked List Implementation Theory\n    - Mathematical Proof:\n    If we store: link = prev ⊕ next\n    Then: prev ⊕ link = prev ⊕ (prev ⊕ next) = (prev ⊕ prev) ⊕ next = 0 ⊕ next = next\n\nTraditional Node: [data][prev_ptr][next_ptr] = 16 bytes (64-bit)\nXOR Node:        [data][xor_link]           = 12 bytes (64-bit)\nMemory Savings:  25% reduction in pointer storage\n*/\n\nclass XORNode {\n    constructor(data) {\n        this.data = data;\n        this.link = 0; // XOR of prev and next addresses\n    }\n}\n\n// Theoretical traversal algorithm\nfunction traverseXORList(head, direction = 'forward') {\n    /*\n    Forward Traversal:\n    prev = 0, current = head\n    while (current !== null):\n        next = prev ⊕ current.link\n        prev = current\n        current = next\n    \n    Mathematical Invariant:\n    At each step: current.link = address(prev) ⊕ address(next)\n    */\n}\n\n// Complexity Analysis\nconst complexityAnalysis = {\n    space: \"O(n) - 25% memory reduction vs doubly linked list\",\n    timeTraversal: \"O(n) - same as regular linked list\",\n    timeInsertion: \"O(1) - but requires address arithmetic\",\n    limitations: [\n        \"Cannot traverse from arbitrary node without context\",\n        \"Debugging complexity increases significantly\",\n        \"Garbage collection complications\",\n        \"Platform-dependent pointer arithmetic\"\n    ]\n};",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- Methematical Foundation:\n    - xor property: a ⊕ a = 0 and a ⊕ 0 = a\n\n- XOR Linked List Implementation Theory\n    - Mathematical Proof:\n    If we store: link = prev ⊕ next\n    Then: prev ⊕ link = prev ⊕ (prev ⊕ next) = (prev ⊕ prev) ⊕ next = 0 ⊕ next = next\n\nTraditional Node: [data][prev_ptr][next_ptr] = 16 bytes (64-bit)\nXOR Node:        [data][xor_link]           = 12 bytes (64-bit)\nMemory Savings:  25% reduction in pointer storage\n*/\n\nclass XORNode {\n    constructor(data) {\n        this.data = data;\n        this.link = 0; // XOR of prev and next addresses\n    }\n}\n\n// Theoretical traversal algorithm\nfunction traverseXORList(head, direction = 'forward') {\n    /*\n    Forward Traversal:\n    prev = 0, current = head\n    while (current !== null):\n        next = prev ⊕ current.link\n        prev = current\n        current = next\n    \n    Mathematical Invariant:\n    At each step: current.link = address(prev) ⊕ address(next)\n    */\n}\n\n// Complexity Analysis\nconst complexityAnalysis = {\n    space: \"O(n) - 25% memory reduction vs doubly linked list\",\n    timeTraversal: \"O(n) - same as regular linked list\",\n    timeInsertion: \"O(1) - but requires address arithmetic\",\n    limitations: [\n        \"Cannot traverse from arbitrary node without context\",\n        \"Debugging complexity increases significantly\",\n        \"Garbage collection complications\",\n        \"Platform-dependent pointer arithmetic\"\n    ]\n};",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
