      "text": "- // Floyd's Algorithm - Mathematical Foundation\n/*\nTHEOREM: If a cycle exists, slow and fast pointers will meet.\n\nPROOF:\nLet:\n- μ = distance from head to cycle start\n- λ = cycle length  \n- k = distance from cycle start to meeting point\n\nPhase 1: Detection\nWhen slow pointer enters cycle, fast pointer is already inside.\nLet fast pointer be 'd' steps ahead of slow pointer in the cycle.\n\nAt each step:\n- Slow moves 1 step\n- Fast moves 2 steps  \n- Gap reduces by 1 step\n\nSince gap = d initially, they meet after d steps.\nMeeting point: k = d mod λ\n\nPhase 2: Finding cycle start\nTHEOREM: Distance from head to cycle start = Distance from meeting point to cycle start\n\nPROOF:\nWhen they meet:\n- Slow traveled: μ + k steps\n- Fast traveled: μ + k + nλ steps (where n ≥ 1)\n\nSince fast moves twice as fast:\n2(μ + k) = μ + k + nλ\n2μ + 2k = μ + k + nλ  \nμ + k = nλ\nμ = nλ - k = (n-1)λ + (λ - k)\n\nThis means: μ ≡ (λ - k) mod λ\n\nTherefore, starting from head and meeting point simultaneously,\nboth pointers will meet exactly at cycle start after μ steps.\n*/\n\nfunction floydAlgorithmWithProof(head) {\n    // Phase 1: Detect cycle\n    let slow = head, fast = head;\n    \n    while (fast && fast.next) {\n        slow = slow.next;\n        fast = fast.next.next;\n        \n        if (slow === fast) {\n            // Cycle detected, now find start\n            \n            // Phase 2: Find cycle start\n            let start = head;\n            while (start !== slow) {\n                start = start.next;\n                slow = slow.next;\n            }\n            \n            return {\n                hasCycle: true,\n                cycleStart: start,\n                proof: \"Mathematical invariant: μ = (n-1)λ + (λ - k)\"\n            };\n        }\n    }\n    \n    return { hasCycle: false };\n}\n\n// Advanced: Finding cycle length\nfunction findCycleLength(meetingPoint) {\n    let length = 1;\n    let current = meetingPoint.next;\n    \n    while (current !== meetingPoint) {\n        current = current.next;\n        length++;\n    }\n    \n    return length;\n} ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- // Floyd's Algorithm - Mathematical Foundation\n/*\nTHEOREM: If a cycle exists, slow and fast pointers will meet.\n\nPROOF:\nLet:\n- μ = distance from head to cycle start\n- λ = cycle length  \n- k = distance from cycle start to meeting point\n\nPhase 1: Detection\nWhen slow pointer enters cycle, fast pointer is already inside.\nLet fast pointer be 'd' steps ahead of slow pointer in the cycle.\n\nAt each step:\n- Slow moves 1 step\n- Fast moves 2 steps  \n- Gap reduces by 1 step\n\nSince gap = d initially, they meet after d steps.\nMeeting point: k = d mod λ\n\nPhase 2: Finding cycle start\nTHEOREM: Distance from head to cycle start = Distance from meeting point to cycle start\n\nPROOF:\nWhen they meet:\n- Slow traveled: μ + k steps\n- Fast traveled: μ + k + nλ steps (where n ≥ 1)\n\nSince fast moves twice as fast:\n2(μ + k) = μ + k + nλ\n2μ + 2k = μ + k + nλ  \nμ + k = nλ\nμ = nλ - k = (n-1)λ + (λ - k)\n\nThis means: μ ≡ (λ - k) mod λ\n\nTherefore, starting from head and meeting point simultaneously,\nboth pointers will meet exactly at cycle start after μ steps.\n*/\n\nfunction floydAlgorithmWithProof(head) {\n    // Phase 1: Detect cycle\n    let slow = head, fast = head;\n    \n    while (fast && fast.next) {\n        slow = slow.next;\n        fast = fast.next.next;\n        \n        if (slow === fast) {\n            // Cycle detected, now find start\n            \n            // Phase 2: Find cycle start\n            let start = head;\n            while (start !== slow) {\n                start = start.next;\n                slow = slow.next;\n            }\n            \n            return {\n                hasCycle: true,\n                cycleStart: start,\n                proof: \"Mathematical invariant: μ = (n-1)λ + (λ - k)\"\n            };\n        }\n    }\n    \n    return { hasCycle: false };\n}\n\n// Advanced: Finding cycle length\nfunction findCycleLength(meetingPoint) {\n    let length = 1;\n    let current = meetingPoint.next;\n    \n    while (current !== meetingPoint) {\n        current = current.next;\n        length++;\n    }\n    \n    return length;\n} ",
