    {
      "id": "ktWOhnZVnk138tz2SrQfR",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3695.19406747818,
      "y": 228.58752155303955,
      "width": 725.9990234375,
      "height": 2700,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 2,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2V",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 564713657,
      "version": 881,
      "versionNonce": 288126519,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1758090081323,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "// Comprehensive Two-Pointer Patterns\n\n// Pattern 1: Finding Middle Element\n/*\nTHEOREM: When fast pointer reaches end, slow pointer is at middle.\n\nPROOF:\nLet n = total nodes\nWhen fast reaches end: fast traveled n-1 steps (0-indexed)\nSlow traveled (n-1)/2 steps\nFor odd n: slow at position (n-1)/2 = middle\nFor even n: slow at position (n-2)/2 = first middle\n*/\nfunction findMiddle(head) {\n    let slow = head, fast = head;\n    \n    while (fast && fast.next) {\n        slow = slow.next;\n        fast = fast.next.next;\n    }\n    \n    return slow; // Mathematical guarantee: middle element\n}\n\n// Pattern 2: Nth from End\n/*\nTHEOREM: Gap of n between pointers ensures correct positioning.\n\nPROOF:\nLet L = list length\nFast pointer starts n steps ahead\nWhen fast reaches end (position L), slow is at position L-n\nThis is exactly the nth node from end.\n*/\nfunction nthFromEnd(head, n) {\n    let fast = head, slow = head;\n    \n    // Create gap of n\n    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        if (!fast) return null; // n > list length\n        fast = fast.next;\n    }\n    \n    // Move both until fast reaches end\n    while (fast) {\n        slow = slow.next;\n        fast = fast.next;\n    }\n    \n    return slow;\n}\n\n// Pattern 3: Palindrome Detection\n/*\nTHEOREM: Reverse second half and compare with first half.\n\nMATHEMATICAL APPROACH:\n1. Find middle using two pointers: O(n/2)\n2. Reverse second half: O(n/2)  \n3. Compare both halves: O(n/2)\nTotal: O(n) time, O(1) space\n*/\nfunction isPalindrome(head) {\n    if (!head || !head.next) return true;\n    \n    // Find middle\n    let slow = head, fast = head;\n    while (fast.next && fast.next.next) {\n        slow = slow.next;\n        fast = fast.next.next;\n    }\n    \n    // Reverse second half\n    let secondHalf = reverseList(slow.next);\n    \n    // Compare\n    let firstHalf = head;\n    while (secondHalf) {\n        if (firstHalf.val !== secondHalf.val) return false;\n        firstHalf = firstHalf.next;\n        secondHalf = secondHalf.next;\n    }\n    \n    return true;\n}\n\n// Pattern 4: Intersection Point\n/*\nTHEOREM: Two pointers with length compensation find intersection.\n\nMATHEMATICAL PROOF:\nLet A = length of list1, B = length of list2, C = common length\nPointer1 travels: A + C + B = A + B + C\nPointer2 travels: B + C + A = A + B + C\nBoth travel same distance, meet at intersection.\n*/\nfunction findIntersection(headA, headB) {\n    if (!headA || !headB) return null;\n    \n    let pA = headA, pB = headB;\n    \n    while (pA !== pB) {\n        pA = pA ? pA.next : headB;\n        pB = pB ? pB.next : headA;\n    }\n    \n    return pA; // Either intersection or null\n}",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "// Comprehensive Two-Pointer Patterns\n\n// Pattern 1: Finding Middle Element\n/*\nTHEOREM: When fast pointer reaches end, slow pointer is at middle.\n\nPROOF:\nLet n = total nodes\nWhen fast reaches end: fast traveled n-1 steps (0-indexed)\nSlow traveled (n-1)/2 steps\nFor odd n: slow at position (n-1)/2 = middle\nFor even n: slow at position (n-2)/2 = first middle\n*/\nfunction findMiddle(head) {\n    let slow = head, fast = head;\n    \n    while (fast && fast.next) {\n        slow = slow.next;\n        fast = fast.next.next;\n    }\n    \n    return slow; // Mathematical guarantee: middle element\n}\n\n// Pattern 2: Nth from End\n/*\nTHEOREM: Gap of n between pointers ensures correct positioning.\n\nPROOF:\nLet L = list length\nFast pointer starts n steps ahead\nWhen fast reaches end (position L), slow is at position L-n\nThis is exactly the nth node from end.\n*/\nfunction nthFromEnd(head, n) {\n    let fast = head, slow = head;\n    \n    // Create gap of n\n    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        if (!fast) return null; // n > list length\n        fast = fast.next;\n    }\n    \n    // Move both until fast reaches end\n    while (fast) {\n        slow = slow.next;\n        fast = fast.next;\n    }\n    \n    return slow;\n}\n\n// Pattern 3: Palindrome Detection\n/*\nTHEOREM: Reverse second half and compare with first half.\n\nMATHEMATICAL APPROACH:\n1. Find middle using two pointers: O(n/2)\n2. Reverse second half: O(n/2)  \n3. Compare both halves: O(n/2)\nTotal: O(n) time, O(1) space\n*/\nfunction isPalindrome(head) {\n    if (!head || !head.next) return true;\n    \n    // Find middle\n    let slow = head, fast = head;\n    while (fast.next && fast.next.next) {\n        slow = slow.next;\n        fast = fast.next.next;\n    }\n    \n    // Reverse second half\n    let secondHalf = reverseList(slow.next);\n    \n    // Compare\n    let firstHalf = head;\n    while (secondHalf) {\n        if (firstHalf.val !== secondHalf.val) return false;\n        firstHalf = firstHalf.next;\n        secondHalf = secondHalf.next;\n    }\n    \n    return true;\n}\n\n// Pattern 4: Intersection Point\n/*\nTHEOREM: Two pointers with length compensation find intersection.\n\nMATHEMATICAL PROOF:\nLet A = length of list1, B = length of list2, C = common length\nPointer1 travels: A + C + B = A + B + C\nPointer2 travels: B + C + A = A + B + C\nBoth travel same distance, meet at intersection.\n*/\nfunction findIntersection(headA, headB) {\n    if (!headA || !headB) return null;\n    \n    let pA = headA, pB = headB;\n    \n    while (pA !== pB) {\n        pA = pA ? pA.next : headB;\n        pB = pB ? pB.next : headA;\n    }\n    \n    return pA; // Either intersection or null\n}",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
